% Three colours for four regions of a map, no two neighbours alike:
% a search problem written as rules.  Every stable model is one valid
% colouring (lesson 5).
%
%   python3 datalog.py --models programs/colouring.dl

region(wa). region(nt). region(sa). region(qld).
colour(red). colour(green). colour(blue).

border(wa, nt).  border(wa, sa).  border(nt, sa).
border(nt, qld). border(sa, qld).

% A choice: each region takes a colour unless it has taken another.
% The two rules lean on each other through `not`, which is what lets
% a program have several models (eligibility-choice.dl, larger).
painted(R, C) :- region(R), colour(C), not other(R, C).
other(R, C)   :- region(R), colour(C), painted(R, D), C != D.

% A test: no model may paint neighbours alike.  `clash` is the barber
% on purpose.  Where a border has one colour on both sides the rule
% says clash holds exactly if it does not, so that model cannot exist.
clash :- border(R, S), painted(R, C), painted(S, C), not clash.
